  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Hey.\nI bet you could save a bunch of storage space on your S3 bucket for avatars by weeding out uploads above a certain ridiculous limit. And by making the S3 reject too big of avatars by default (and inform the user about the limit and link to a Doc page explaining audio compression settings as well as Crunch compression). Why especially on the S3? Because a limit on VRCSDK would probably get modded away by a bunch. With a limit in place old avatars with too big sizes could be deleted in hindsight.\nHow about a limit of 200MB just like it's already in the client? (Btw the limit is still broken today https://feedback.vrchat.com/bug-reports/p/safety-maximum-avatar-download-size-doesnt-work).\nThank you for your time.",
